{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1363354-question-about-dark-eras-2","id":1363354,"title":"Question about Dark Eras 2?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-01-25T15:00:52-08:00","id":1363354,"title":"Question about Dark Eras 2?","content":"Is Duat one of the Dead Dominions (like it says in Dark Eras 2) or is it in the Lower Depths (like I think it says in Mummy: the Curse 2E)? Or are there two Duats? I like it better in the Dead Dominions, but what do you guys think?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-25T15:15:39-08:00","id":1363356,"title":"","content":"What DE2 says (unless you refer to something else) is that Sin-Eaters <i>believe</i> Duat is a Dead Dominion, which is quite natural considering that they have no good reference for Duat and the Underworld sounds quite close if that's what you can perceive yourself and where the dead obviously go.<br /> It's also fully possible that there is a Dead Dominion styled after Duat, just like there are Dead Dominions styled after Hell, Valhalla, Limbo, Hades, etc, but Dead Dominions are generally not considered to actually be the afterlives that they portray from an OOC perspective.<br /> <br /> The Duat mummies talk about and visit is described in surprising amount of detail in Mummy 2e. It's not in the Underworld, and would be referred to as a Lower Depth by a mage.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-25T19:17:05-08:00","id":1363383,"title":"","content":"The general rule is to assume a plurality unless a singular existence is particularly noted.<br /> <br /> Duat is not a Dead Dominion, however. It doesn't exist in the Underworld, and it deals with souls more so than ghosts.<br /> <br /> But hey, there's a Mictlan with Anubis in it, so there's probably <i>a</i> Duat in the Underworld. It's just not <i>the</i> Duat.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-25T19:41:11-08:00","id":1363386,"title":"","content":"Thank you for clarifying that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-25T19:43:53-08:00","id":1363388,"title":"","content":"Are the Dead Dominions kind of like the Far Shores in Wraith?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-25T20:07:58-08:00","id":1363394,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Penelope</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1363354-question-about-dark-eras-2?p=1363388#post1363388\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Are the Dead Dominions kind of like the Far Shores in Wraith?</div> </div> </div> </div>Dead Dominions are ultimately-temporary places of refuge for the dead beyond the Rivers of Death, perched above the identity-dissolving Ocean of Fragments. If you're a ghost who's lost all their Anchors and been largely forgotten by the living, you have a few options for surviving the Underworld:<br /> <br /> 1. Sift the Castoffs that drift down the tributary streams that trickle through the Upper Reaches into the Rivers for cruelty-free ectophagia. (It's a living.)<br /> 2. Stalk the tunnels for other ghosts to engage in <i>non</i>-cruelty-free ectophagia. (It works better for some than others.)<br /> 3. Acquire a deathmask, become a Reaper, and serve the Chthonic Gods. (The dead belong below.)<br /> 4. Drink the waters of a River, survive the horrible pain and the terrible mutilation, and become a geist. (The social scene is not as engaging.)<br /> 5. Pay a Ferryman to take you across the Rivers to one of the Dead Dominions, where you'll get enough Essence every day to keep the Underworld from eating you as long as you follow the Old Laws. (You may or may not be hastening the place's destruction by coming there.)<br /> <br /> Options 3 and 4 have some synergy with Option 2 and nothing strictly ever stops you from Option 1 until you've crossed the River, but Option 5 is the one with the most gravity that doesn't involve getting the ability to freely leave the Underworld outright, which would be relatively innocuous if not for the fact that the Old Laws and the Kerberoi who enforce them can get Really Fucking Weird.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-25T21:43:09-08:00","id":1363407,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar111_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"111\" data-vbnamecard=\"111\">Satchel</a> That definitely answers my question. Thank you \ud83d\ude0a.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-25T23:42:50-08:00","id":1363416,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Penelope</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1363354-question-about-dark-eras-2?p=1363388#post1363388\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Are the Dead Dominions kind of like the Far Shores in Wraith?</div> </div> </div> </div>in that they are various weird afterworlds that ghosts who have moved beyond their twilight existence alongside the living might travel to reach, yes.<br /> <br /> But thematically the Far Shores (when they\u2019re not corrupted) are supposed to be places that help a Wraith achieve Transcendence. In contrast, the Dead Domains are places that ghosts end up when they\u2019re trying to hold on. Geist doesn\u2019t make a big distinction between enlightened transcendence, and obliviation like Wraith does (in part because in Geist, ghosts aren\u2019t souls). Dissolution of the self is dissolution of the self.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-26T05:25:08-08:00","id":1363436,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1098_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1098\" data-vbnamecard=\"1098\">glamourweaver</a> thanks. That makes sense.<br /> <br /> I wonder if Charon overthrew Hades to become ruler of the Underworld. In mythology he started out as Hades\u2019s servant. (Not that I\u2019m ever gonna play Wraith anyway, my bf doesn\u2019t even like when I play Changeling once a week, but it\u2019s interesting to think about.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-26T11:25:17-08:00","id":1363485,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Penelope</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1363354-question-about-dark-eras-2?p=1363436#post1363436\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1098_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1098\" data-vbnamecard=\"1098\">glamourweaver</a> thanks. That makes sense.<br /> <br /> I wonder if Charon overthrew Hades to become ruler of the Underworld. In mythology he started out as Hades\u2019s servant. (Not that I\u2019m ever gonna play Wraith anyway, my bf doesn\u2019t even like when I play Changeling once a week, but it\u2019s interesting to think about.)</div> </div> </div> </div>In Wraith context, Hades would be a Shining One ruler of a Far Shore back when Charon led the Ferrymen, taking wraiths across the Sunless Sea to those realms.<br /> <br /> Of course the other Ferrymen rebel led against Charon after the First Great Maelstrom with the Fall of Rome, when Charon declared himself Imperator with Stygia\u2019s refounding instead of reforming the Republic. And then Charon broke relations with the Far Shores in the late Middle Ages/Early Mosern Era when it became clear that at least some of them had become corrupt, and the believers in said afterworlds were criminalized as \u201cHeretics\u201d.<br /> <br /> So Hades &amp;/or Persephone could still be reigning over some Far Shores, but Charon stopped shepherding souls to them long long ago.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":1098,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","user":"glamourweaver","date":". 01-27-2020, 02:36 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-26T17:52:29-08:00","id":1363542,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1098_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1098\" data-vbnamecard=\"1098\">glamourweaver</a> once again, that makes a lot of sense. Thank you \ud83d\ude0a.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]}]}